meta {
  name: Scan
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/entry-guard/scan
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~tickers: AAPL,MSFT,TSLA
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Entry Guard — Scan
  
  Evaluates tickers against the universal entry guard and returns which ones
  currently PASS. Read-only diagnostic: it runs the exact logic that gates every
  BUY, under the current webull.entry-guard.* config, so results match what the
  bot would allow right now. Does NOT arm tickers or place orders.
  
  ## Query
  - `tickers` — optional comma-separated symbols to scan instead of the
    watchlist (e.g. AAPL,MSFT,TSLA). Any US symbol works. Omit to scan the
    configured watchlist.
  
  ## Response (200)
  { guardConfig: { enabled, supertrendTimespan, emaTimespan, emaFast, emaMid,
                   emaSlow, emaRequireMid, conditionLogic },
    scanned, passedCount,
    passed: [ ...tickers that passed... ],
    results: [ { ticker, passed, reason } ],
    mode, timestamp }
  
  The `reason` explains a failure (e.g. ST_NOT_UP_M15, EMA_STACK_FAIL(...),
  ST_UNAVAILABLE_M15, or OR_BOTH_FAIL[...]). `passed` is the list you want.
  
  ## Errors
  - `400` — nothing to scan (empty watchlist and no ?tickers=).
}
